\fs20\b ILLUSTRATIVE EXAMPLE \'96 NOT LEGAL ADVICE.\b0\par
Drafting aid only. Every term must be tailored to the offender and the evidence, and settled with your prosecutor / legal services. Source: Thinking About Policing.\par
\par
\fs28\b CRIMINAL BEHAVIOUR ORDER \'96 EXAMPLE TERMS\b0\fs20\par
\i Anti-social Behaviour, Crime and Policing Act 2014, section 22 (made on conviction)\i0\par
\par
\b Drafting principles (from the case law)\b0\par
Terms must be reasonable, proportionate, realistic, practical, clear and enforceable (\i Boness\i0 [2005] EWCA Crim 2395), and "policeable" \'96 capable of being understood and monitored by the offender, the police and the public (\i R v Maguire\i0 [2019] EWCA Crim 1193). A CBO is not to be imposed lightly. Define any area with an attached map. Avoid vague terms such as "behaving in an anti-social manner".\par
\par
\b Example prohibitions (illustrative \'96 select and tailor)\b0\par
\tab 1. Not to enter any [named retailer] store in England and Wales.\par
\tab 2. Not to enter the area edged red on the attached map (Schedule A).\par
\tab 3. Not to enter any retail premises from which you have been formally banned and made aware of the ban.\par
\tab 4. Not to be in possession of [specified item, e.g. a holdall lined to defeat security tags] in a public place.\par
\tab 5. Not to contact or associate with [named individual(s)] in a public place.\par
\par
\b Example positive requirement\b0\par
\tab 6. To attend and engage with [named drug/alcohol or support programme] as directed by [agency].\par
\par
\b Duration\b0\par
For an adult, a minimum of 2 years with no statutory maximum; for a person under 18, between 1 and 3 years. State a clear start and end date. (Requirements should name the person/agency responsible for supervising compliance.)\par
\par
\b Check before you ask for it\b0\par
Each term: necessary? proportionate to the harm? clear enough to police? Does it avoid needless interference with work, education or other court orders?\par
